The three sanctuaries are: * ''Kashiko-dokoro'' (賢所) – the central shrine, dedicated to the mythological ancestress of the [[Imperial Family of Japan|Imperial Family]], [[Amaterasu]]. (Since 1915, special [[rolling stock]] for the ceremonial use of the imperial family is known as ''Kashiko-dokoro Jōgyosha'' (賢所乗御車) from the name of this sanctuary.) The ''[[Yasakani no magatama]]'' or Sacred Jewel, one of the [[Imperial Regalia of Japan]], is also said to be housed in the Kashiko-dokoro. * ''Kōrei-den'' (皇霊殿) – the Ancestral Spirits Sanctuary, enshrining the departed spirits of the Imperial Family from one year after their death. * ''Shin-den'' (神殿) – the Sanctuary of the ''[[Kami]]'', enshrining the ''Amatsukami'' (天津神) from [[Takama-ga-hara]] and the ''Kunitsukami'' (国津神) from [[Japanese mythology]].
